From d349fc015a644ea999dd2e018e0b2070d4270883 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shi Jiayang <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:57:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_wed: support MT7987 WED v3.1

MT7987 implements WED v3.1 without the WO microcontroller present on
MT7986 and MT7988. Describe its register layout and WO capability
separately and add its TX buffer manager, interrupt, DMA reset and
RRO v3.1 receive paths. Export the hardware version and RRO ring setup
operations required by mt76, with a configuration-safe version helper.

Rebase the functional WED SDK series onto Linux 6.18, preserving the
upstream fixes already present for legacy hardware and descriptor-based
ring ownership. In particular, freeing RX rings never depends on a
TX ring's configured flag, and partially allocated rings are released.
Retain the WPDMA busy result across reset helpers and unwind AMSDU
allocation failures so module removal and reinsertion remain safe.
Provide compact v3.1 register and capability diagnostics in debugfs.

Propagate TX pool allocation failures through reset_dma after stopping
the engines and cleaning partial allocations. Clear pool state on free
so a retry or detach cannot unmap stale DMA addresses, and never restart
WED with an empty pool.

Free both receive pools when HWRRO page allocation fails, including
buffers owned by the WLAN driver, and clear the HWRRO state for a retry
or detach. Clear the WO pointer after deinitialization so a failed
reinsertion cannot deinitialize stale WO queues a second time.

Quiesce the WED v3.1 WPDMA drivers and interrupt agent, then stop and
drain its separate RRO receive descriptor driver and prefetcher before
the caller resets WLAN or frees receive buffers. Cover the v3.0
indication/page mode supported by v3.1 hardware, and restore its receive
processing on start. Leave WED v1/v2/v3 stop paths unchanged.

Based on MediaTek SDK patches by Rex Lu <rex.lu@mediatek.com>, including
commit 0b119d4c2711133024fa3eedfa34004e1d3cc915, as integrated and rebased
by huimin.he <huimin.he@cybertan.com.tw>. The SDK's expanded debugfs dump
is omitted in favor of the existing diagnostics.

Signed-off-by: Shi Jiayang <shi05275@163.com>
